# The languages this project ships translations for, one per line, as
# `po/<language>.po` and `<language>` in a locale directory (the convention
# `msgfmt --desktop -d po` and `msgfmt --xml -d po` read too, so the desktop
# file and the metainfo can be generated with the languages merged).
#
# English is the source language and is not listed: it is the `.pot` itself
# (`po/pixlay.pot`, extracted by `po/extract-pot`), so a language here is a
# translation added on top of it, and this file plus `po/<language>.po` is the
# whole of what one costs. Nothing depends on a language being listed — an
# unlisted one is simply not built and not installed, and every string falls
# back to its English source (`crates/pixlay/tests/i18n.rs` holds a listed
# language to the template: complete, no `fuzzy`, placeholders kept).
zh_CN
